{{steps.implement.output}}

The workflow ran check again after that step: ok = {{steps.verify.output.ok}}, exit {{steps.verify.output.exitCode}}. The end of its output:
{{steps.verify.output.output}}

Write the handoff for RUN-{{steps.read.output.run}} from spec/runs/TEMPLATE-handoff.md (read it with repo.read): every section, the verification transcript quoting the check output above, and Known gaps naming each unmet definition-of-done item by number. Then update STATUS.md in the repository with repo.write so its current-run line reads RUN-{{steps.read.output.run}}: awaiting verification @ <sha>, where <sha> is the newest commit git.log shows. Answer with the handoff document itself, as Markdown, and nothing else.

